","position":"1788428415168670001-81a2cbce-a44d-4e92-b4bf-c252cfc9b4f1"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"058ec124481f1fd34cea13ffadd8e91c2c29178cc31241a908097176516f1f9e","event_uuid":"ef3e7d21-d3c5-4465-a464-52bee8604278","position":{"commit_sha":"194700601c20dc8168d1bcb2757100187d3ccee6","position":"1788428466347374001-ef3e7d21-d3c5-4465-a464-52bee8604278"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"f2186b2acc7901e0b247f6b6eb0bb14e61aef537686d2d3866980f829cf41cef","event_uuid":"d6c1c40c-02f9-4c0e-b83a-f385715f3ea5","position":{"commit_sha":"615ef85e0ae20f283c7262358b8a143fe61fcc57","position":"1788428743059008001-d6c1c40c-02f9-4c0e-b83a-f385715f3ea5"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"859150315ddbb3e36555b9b004afb8c7a878a95b6cf5570c65528d1b94207186","event_uuid":"fe02f938-de51-45f1-88ef-761099d27776","position":{"commit_sha":"6bd5d8759dd3f30235974db400158d8eaf74fd25","position":"1788428749581534001-fe02f938-de51-45f1-88ef-761099d27776"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Implemented the shared Jira-family link canonicalizer in rebar_reconciler.link_direction and collapsed both Cloud/DC map_remote_links methods to thin delegation. Added RED-first coverage for standalone loading, outward/inward/symmetric/unmapped/fallback/dedup cases, backend delegation, and parity against the captured issuelinks fixture. Validation: focused link suites green, make lint green, make typecheck green, and pytest -m 'not integration and not external' -x -q reached only the known baseline lifecycle failure after 1303 passes.","timestamp":1788425471670719001}],"completion_expectation":"required","created_at":1788311582971759001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"1870a992-41ff-44a8-99c8-69b41d0b8624","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"0fcb-b65e-1c82-4a4d"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\n\n`JiraBackend.map_remote_links` (`src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/adapters/jira/backend.py:319-357`) and `JiraDataCenterBackend.map_remote_links` (`adapters/jira_datacenter/backend.py:529-559`) duplicate the same vendor-payload parsing, fallback, direction resolution, deduplication, and observation construction. Direction already has its core-root source of truth in `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/link_direction.py` beside `resolve_inbound_link`; the duplicate adapter logic risks Cloud/DC drift around that seam.\n\n## End State\n\nA pure canonicalizer in `rebar_reconciler.link_direction` turns Jira `issuelinks` into the existing `(relation | None, remote_key, opaque_vendor_type)` observations. It reuses `resolve_inbound_link`, preserves the direction-agnostic fallback for unmapped/malformed-but-keyed types, and de-duplicates by `(vendor_type, remote_key)`. Both Cloud and Data Center adapters retain their own transports and simply delegate. The provider-neutral desired-versus-observed relation diff is unchanged.\n\n## Implementation Plan\n\n1. Add the canonicalizer to `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/link_direction.py`, beside `resolve_inbound_link`, rather than to `adapters/jira_family/`. That core-root placement permits the required core direction ownership without reversing the adapters-to-core dependency boundary.\n2. Keep `link_direction.py` stdlib-only: reconciler tests and isolated execution load it by `spec_from_file_location`, so the new function may not import adapter, package, or third-party dependencies.\n3. Replace both adapter method bodies with thin delegation while retaining each adapter's transport and external protocol behavior. Do not change the provider-neutral differ, link mutation payloads, or relation vocabulary.\n4. Add shared vectors and adapter-delegation coverage for outward/inward links, symmetric relations, unmapped types, malformed entries, fallback keys, duplicate entries, and empty input; run the same expectations through both backends and a standalone module-load test.\n\n## File Impact\n\n- `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/link_direction.py` — canonical core-root parser/normalizer\n- `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/adapters/jira/backend.py` and `adapters/jira_datacenter/backend.py` — thin Cloud/DC delegation only\n- focused link-direction, Cloud, Data Center, shared-vector, and standalone-loader tests/fixtures\n\nCascade flag: true. Recensus semantic, string, dynamic-import, and monkeypatch consumers before moving behavior.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [x] `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/link_direction.py` owns one pure canonicalizer next to `resolve_inbound_link`; no canonicalizer is added under `adapters/jira_family/`.\n- [x] The core module remains stdlib-only and loads successfully through its standalone `spec_from_file_location` path.\n- [x] Cloud and Data Center retain separate transports and delegate to the same core canonicalizer without importing a provider-specific implementation into core.\n- [x] Both adapters return byte/shape-equivalent canonical observations for shared outward, inward, symmetric, unmapped, malformed, fallback-key, duplicate, and empty-input vectors.\n- [x] The canonicalizer preserves current direction semantics and the `(vendor_type, remote_key)` de-duplication/fallback behavior, including `relation=None` for an unmapped vendor type with a recoverable peer key.\n- [x] Provider-neutral relation contracts, desired-versus-observed diff behavior, and Jira mutation payload behavior remain unchanged.\n- [x] Focused core/adapter/standalone-loader tests plus lint, typecheck, module-size, and complexity gates pass.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/link_direction.py","reason":"own the shared pure Jira-family link canonicalizer beside resolve_inbound_link"},{"path":"src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/adapters/jira/backend.py","reason":"delegate Cloud link normalization to the shared core canonicalizer"},{"path":"src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/adapters/jira_datacenter/backend.py","reason":"delegate Data Center link normalization to the shared core canonicalizer"},{"path":"tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/diffing/test_jira_link_canonicalizer_a07a.py","reason":"cover standalone loading, delegation, fallback, and captured Jira vectors"},{"path":"tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/diffing/test_link_direction_absolute.py","reason":"preserve absolute direction contracts for the shared canonicalizer owner"},{"path":"tests/fixtures/jira/issuelinks_map.json","reason":"shared Cloud/DC behavior vectors read by the parity test"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[["parent","78f2-b104-e3c9-4b86"],["relates_to","0fcb-b65e-1c82-4a4d"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"78f2-b104-e3c9-4b86","parent_status_uuid":"d6c1c40c-02f9-4c0e-b83a-f385715f3ea5","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":1,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"closed","tags":["janitor","jira","architecture","rp10"],"ticket_id":"a07a-5eeb-1223-491c","ticket_type":"story","title":"Centralize Jira-family link canonicalization across Cloud and Data Center","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["a895240d-7b4b-4944-8c2d-39c7d1249171","5dd1afc1-24f6-43ba-9741-0298d05291c9","2ecdfa8b-5183-4733-b882-4f1f89ac6b8c","fb937149-3193-4f55-8015-295a396f6a4f","2747fb9c-3b77-44b5-ad04-2c72605a2ced","796a7582-4118-4f93-8e9b-165a960a9f1f","1870a992-41ff-44a8-99c8-69b41d0b8624","81a2cbce-a44d-4e92-b4bf-c252cfc9b4f1","ef3e7d21-d3c5-4465-a464-52bee8604278","d6c1c40c-02f9-4c0e-b83a-f385715f3ea5","fe02f938-de51-45f1-88ef-761099d27776"]},"env_id":"","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1788437993388417663,"uuid":"31acda5b-d4ea-4fd0-928c-2cf7ab54f8c4"}